title: 'statement-store: add statement/4 with the set reconciliation messages'
doc:
- audience: [Node Operator, Node Dev]
  description: |-
    A node with `--statement-dht` now offers `statement/4` and falls back to `statement/3`,
    `statement/2` and `statement/1`. A node without the flag does not change. `statement/4`
    carries the `statement/3` messages and two messages of set reconciliation: an announce of
    short hashes with a salt, and an answer with one bit for each announced hash. The node decodes
    both and drops them, and nothing sends them yet.
    A peer that lists `statement/3` in its identify answer still joins the DHT index, and two
    nodes settle on `statement/3` when one of them runs an older build.
crates:
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: patch
